[DISPLAY WHEN - Display Installation Options]
$C ===================================================================================================${Reset}
$Y                                On2it-WinFixIT$W - INSTALLATION OPTIONS${Reset}
$C ===================================================================================================${Reset}
${W} When installing Windows 11 using On2it-WinFixIT${Reset}, you have two distinct paths 
 depending on how you start the installer:

${Y} Installing from within Windows${Reset}
 If you're currently running Windows and launch On2it-WinFixIT from your desktop:
    - You can choose to keep your existing files, apps, and settings.
    - This is ideal if your system is working well and you simply 
      want to refresh or repair Windows.
    - You'll be guided through options like:
        - Keep everything (files, apps, settings)
        - Keep personal files only
        - Wipe everything and start fresh

${Y} Installing by booting from USB${Reset}
 If you restart your computer and boot directly from the USB stick:
    - You'll enter a special lightweight mode called the 
     $W Windows Preinstallation Environment, or WinPE${Reset}.
    - WinPE is designed for clean installs and recovery ONLY.  
      It doesn't load a full Windows system.
    - In this mode, you can only perform a full clean install.
     $W All files, apps, and settings will be erased.${Reset}

${W} WHICH SHOULD YOU CHOOSE?${Reset}
    - If your system is working and you want flexibility - Start from Windows
    - If your system is damaged or you want a clean slate - Boot from USB

 On2it-WinFixIT will guide you through the correct steps based on how you started.
 You'll always be shown clear choices before anything is installed.

[CLEAR]$Y Press ANY Key to continue...$Reset
$C ===================================================================================================${Reset}
$Y                                BEFORE YOU BEGIN - BACKUP YOUR DATA!${Reset} 
$C ===================================================================================================${Reset}

 ${W}Before installing Windows 11 - whether you're keeping your files or starting fresh,
 ${W}it is strongly recommended that you$Y create a backup$W of anything important.${Reset}

 Even if you choose to keep your files and apps:
   - Mistakes can happen.
   - Power interruptions, disk errors, or unexpected issues during installation may result in data loss.

 If you choose a full clean install:
   - All files, apps, and settings will be permanently erased.
   - There is no undo once the process begins.

 WHAT TO BACK UP:
   - Documents, photos, and personal files
   - Emails, browser bookmarks, and saved passwords
   - Any app data or configuration files
   - Anything stored on the Desktop or Downloads folder

 You can use an external USB drive, cloud storage, or a network location - whatever suits your setup.

 On2it-WinFixIT will not begin installation until you confirm your choice, 
 but it cannot recover lost data. Taking a backup now ensures peace of mind later.

[CLEAR] $Y Press ANY Key to continue...$Reset
[DISPLAY WHEN - Run from within Windows]
$C =====================================================================================================${Reset}
$Y                          On2it-WinFixIT$W - INSTALLING from within Windows${Reset}
$C =====================================================================================================${Reset}

$W You have started On2it-WinFixIT from within a full Windows environment.${Reset}
 This gives you the widest range of installation choices:
   -$W Keep everything${Reset}, preserves your files, apps, and settings.
   -$W Keep personal files only${Reset},removes apps and resets settings.
   -$W Wipe everything${Reset},performs a full clean install, removing all files, apps, and settings.

 Even from within Windows, you can choose a full clean install if you want a fresh start.

$W Before proceeding, it is strongly recommended that you BACKUP AMY IMPORTANT DATA!${Reset}
 For, even if you choose to keep files, unexpected issues can still cause data loss.

[DISPLAY WHEN - Booted from USB]
$C ==================================================================================================${Reset}
$Y                                On2it-WinFixIT$W - INSTALLING from USB Boot${Reset}
$C ==================================================================================================${Reset}

$W You have started On2it-WinFixIT by booting from the USB.${reset}

 So, WinFixIT has to run in $W WinPE${Reset}  the $W W${Reset}indows $W P${Reset}reinstallation $WE${Reset}nvironment.  
 WinPE is a lightweight environment designed specifically for Windows' Installation.  
 WinPE does NOT have all the functionality of Windows itself.  

$W In WinPE:${Reset}
$W   - You can only perform a full clean install -$R All FILES, APPS, and SETTINGS will be erased.${Reset}

$W To keep FILES, APPS, and SETTINGS${Reset}, you HAVE to run Windows Setup from a full installation 
 of Windows.  So you should:
$W   - RESTART your machine${Reset} and let it boot into Windows,
$W   - OPEN the USB-INSTALL Partition on the USB${Reset}, and
$W   - Double-Click RUN - On2it-WinFixIT.bat${Reset}.

$W Before proceeding, it is strongly recommended that you BACKUP AnY IMPORTANT DATA!${Reset}

